<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=transformer">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transformer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A transformer transfers electrical energy between circuits through a varying magnetic flux in a shared core. The first type to see wide use was the induction coil, invented by the Rev. Nicholas Callan of Maynooth College, Ireland, in 1836. Yablochkov's lighting system of 1876 used induction coils as transformers, and Gaulard and Gibbs exhibited a secondary generator in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1882. The Hungarian engineers Zipernowsky, Bláthy and Déri designed closed-core transformers in 1884 and patented them in 1885, which made AC distribution practical.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transformer.jpg" alt="Transformer" width="330" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raimond Spekking · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philips_N4422_without_background.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1836</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Maynooth, Ireland</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Nicholas Callan</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Efficient, practical transformer designs did not appear until the 1880s: the closed-core design of Zipernowsky, Bláthy and Déri dates from 1884–1885.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/voltaic-pile">Electric battery<span>1800</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/electromagnetic-induction">Electromagnetic induction<span>1831</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=transformer">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
